Q: Need help filtering proxyAddresses by domain in a specific OU A: <p>The issue you are having is with the regex pattern.</p>
<p>Please see the below update to your script:</p>
<p>I have update the regex match from <code>&quot;^smtp:.*@${domain}$&quot;</code> to <code>&quot;^SMTP:.+@$domain&quot;</code></p>
<pre><code>Import-Module ActiveDirectory

$ou = &quot;OU=Users,DC=contoso,DC=com&quot;
$domain = &quot;domain.co.uk&quot;
$outCsv = &quot;C:\Temp\smtp_proxies.csv&quot;

Get-ADUser -SearchBase $ou -SearchScope Subtree -LDAPFilter &quot;(proxyAddresses=*@${domain})&quot; -Properties proxyAddresses |
ForEach-Object {
    $sam = $_.SamAccountName


    $matches = $_.proxyAddresses | Where-Object {$_ -match &quot;^SMTP:.+@$domain&quot;}

    foreach ($addr in $matches) {
        [pscustomobject]@{
            SamAccountName = $sam
            ProxyAddress   = $addr
        }
    }
} | Export-Csv -Path $outCsv -NoTypeInformation -Encoding UTF8

Write-Host &quot;Export done:&quot; $outCsv
</code></pre>

Q: How to create a type-deducing tuple with neither copyable nor movable members? The tuple itself is a class member A: <p>When type is not movable/copyable, and you want to use them in initializer_list, one way it to use intermediate class which store the parameter, and build the class &quot;on demand&quot;:</p>
<pre><code>template &lt;typename T, typename...Ts&gt;
struct SFactory
{
    using type = S&lt;T&gt;;

    SFactory(Ts... args) : m_params(std::move(args)...) {}

    operator type() const { return std::make_from_tuple&lt;S&lt;T&gt;&gt;(m_params); }

    std::tuple&lt;Ts...&gt; m_params;
};

// There are no partial CTAD
template &lt;typename T, typename...Ts&gt;
SFactory&lt;T, Ts...&gt; MakeSFactory(Ts... args) { return {args...}; }

// To convert tuple of factories to tuple of S
template &lt;typename... SFactories&gt;
std::tuple&lt;typename SFactories::type...&gt; ToTupleOfS(const std::tuple&lt;SFactories...&gt;&amp; factories)
{
    return factories;
}
</code></pre>
<p>Then</p>
<pre><code>auto MakeContainerOfS() {
    return ToTupleOfS(std::tuple(MakeSFactory&lt;int&gt;(1, 41), MakeSFactory&lt;float&gt;(2.1f) /*...*/));
}
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/nKqqb818M" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
<p>Unfortunately, msvc doesn't support that, but accepts that version:</p>
<pre><code>auto MakeContainerOfS() {
    return std::tuple(MakeSFactory&lt;int&gt;(1, 41), MakeSFactory&lt;float&gt;(2.1f) /*...*/);
}

struct Container {
    decltype(ToTupleOfS(MakeContainerOfS())) container{MakeContainerOfS()};
    // ...
};
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/shYvf3sYd" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Demo</a></p>
